      <title>AI cybersecurity is not proof of work</title>
      <link>https://antirez.com/news/163</link>
      <description>📝 The proof of work is the wrong analogy: finding hash collisions, while exponentially harder with N, is guaranteed to find, with enough work, some S so that H(S) satisfies N, so an asymmetry of resources used will see the side with more "work ability" eventually winning. Different LLMs executions take different branches, but eventually the possible branches based on the code possible states are saturated. * Don't trust who says that weak models can find the OpenBSD SACK bug.

🔗 Read more: https://antirez.com/news/163</description>
